};
---

<Layout
  title="Meta Agency: Paid Ads, Advantage+, Organic, UGC & Avatars | hubStudio"
  description="Full-service Meta agency and creative studio: Instagram, Facebook & Threads management, Advantage+ media buying, CAPI attribution, creator whitelisting, studio UGC and AI avatars."
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />

  <div class="prog" aria-hidden="true"><span class="prog__bar"></span></div>

  <div class="page">
    <!-- S1 · HERO -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero__panel">
        <svg class="hero__reg" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
          <path d="M50 4v92M4 50h92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        </svg>
        <div class="hero__panel-in">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r">
            <span class="kicker__tick"></span>Platform
            <span class="kicker__sep">/</span> Meta
          </p>
          <h1 class="hero__title">
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">Organic, Advantage+,</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i serif">creators & commerce.</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">Plus AIGC at scale.</span></span>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero__tag r" style="--d:.45s">
            Content. Paid Ads. Creators. Shops. <em>Avatars.</em>
          </p>
          <div class="hero__lead r" style="--d:.55s">
            <p>
              hubStudio is a full-service Meta agency and creative production studio. We manage your Instagram, Facebook and Threads channels, run full-funnel paid media across Advantage+ with server-side CAPI attribution, manage creator seeding and Partnership Ads whitelisting, operate Meta Shops and enriched catalogs, and produce high-velocity studio UGC and brand-owned AI avatars.
            </p>
            <p>
              Instead of splitting your Meta growth across a social shop, a media buyer, a UGC marketplace and an AI vendor, everything runs under one brief, one creative director and one performance dashboard.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__cta r" style="--d:.65s">
            <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Send the brief</Button>
            <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href="#proof">
              See the work
              <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero__meta r" style="--d:.72s">
            Global Meta operations <span>/</span> Organic, Advantage+, Creators, Shops & Studio
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__visual">
        <img
          src="/Images/meta-hero.jpg"
          alt="A close editorial portrait of a hand holding a phone in warm rim light, the phone screen filled with a paused Instagram Reels frame including the vertical Reels interface elements at the side and bottom."
          width="1024"
          height="1024"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <span class="hero__chip">Platform work <span>/</span> Meta</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cbar" aria-hidden="true">
      {colourBar.map((c) => <span style={`background:${c}`}></span>)}
    </div>

    <!-- S2 · WHY -->
    <section class="why">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="why__top">
          <div class="why__head">
            <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Why it matters</p>
            <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
              Creative is the new<br /><span class="serif">targeting on Meta</span>.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="why__text">
            <p class="r" style="--d:.1s">
              Most brands still run Meta as a set of disconnected jobs: a social agency posting to the grid, a performance buyer starving in Ads Manager for fresh hooks, a UGC broker chasing creators for usage rights, and an e-commerce manager nursing a broken catalog feed.
            </p>
            <p class="r" style="--d:.16s">
              On modern Meta, media buying and creative velocity cannot be separated. Advantage+ relies on first-party CAPI signals and dozens of distinct creative angles to find new pockets of buyers. hubStudio unites organic channel management, full-funnel Meta Ads buying, creator whitelisting, social commerce and high-volume studio + AIGC production under one roof.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="why__shot crop r-clip">
          <div class="crop__inner">
            <img
              src="/Images/meta-roots.jpg"
              alt="A wide editorial shot of two designers at a daylit studio table, four laptop screens lined up showing the Instagram Feed, an Instagram Reels frame, the Meta Ads Manager creative library and an Instagram Stories sequence, one per service lane."
              width="1408"
              height="768"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="fig">Organic, Paid Media, Creators, Commerce & AIGC under one roof</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="stats">
          <p class="stats__quote r">
            One integrated team handles organic channels, Advantage+ media buying, creator whitelisting, catalog commerce and studio creative, with new short-form cuts ready in 48 hours.
          </p>
          <div class="stats__grid">
            {
              stats.map((s, i) => (
                <div class="stat r" style={`--d:${i * 0.1}s`}>
                  <span
                    class="stat__num"
                    data-from={s.from}
                    data-to={s.to}
                    data-suffix={s.suffix}
                  >
                    {s.from}{s.suffix}
                  </span>
                  <span class="stat__label">{s.label}</span>
                  <span class="stat__note">{s.note}</span>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- S3 · COVERAGE -->
    <section class="cover">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Full-stack Meta capabilities</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Everything you need to win <span class="serif">on Meta</span>.
          </h2>
        </header>

        {
          coverage.map((c, i) => (
            <article class={`feature ${i % 2 === 1 ? 'feature--rev' : ''}`}>
              <figure class="feature__media crop r-clip">
                <div class="crop__inner">
                  <img
                    src={c.image}
                    alt={c.alt}
                    width="1024"
                    height="1024"
                    loading="lazy"
                  />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="fig">{c.label} lane</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <div class="feature__body">
                <p class="feature__idx r"><span class="feature__tick"></span>Practice</p>
                <h3 class="dh dh--sm r" style="--d:.05s">{c.heading}</h3>
                {c.lead && <p class="feature__lead r" style="--d:.1s">{c.lead}</p>}
                {c.body.map((para, pi) => (
                  <p class="feature__p r" style={`--d:${0.12 + pi * 0.06}s`}>
                    {para}
                  </p>
                ))}
                <p class="feature__scope r" style="--d:.24s">In scope</p>
                <ul class="chips r" style="--d:.28s">
                  {c.tags.map((t) => (
                    <li class="chip">{t}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }

        <div class="matrix">
          <header class="matrix__head">
            <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Complete service catalog</p>
            <h3 class="dh dh--sm r" style="--d:.05s">
              Six Meta practices, modular or <span class="serif">end to end</span>.
            </h3>
            <p class="matrix__sub r" style="--d:.1s">
              Engage us for full-service Meta agency management across Instagram, Facebook, Threads and WhatsApp, or plug specific media buying, creator whitelisting or studio AIGC lanes into your in-house growth team.
            </p>
          </header>
          <div class="matrix__grid">
            {
              servicePillars.map((p, i) => (
                <article class="mcard r" style={`--d:${(i % 3) * 0.07}s`}>
                  <p class="mcard__eyebrow">{p.eyebrow}</p>
                  <h4 class="mcard__title">{p.title}</h4>
                  <p class="mcard__desc">{p.desc}</p>
                  <ul class="mcard__list">
                    {p.items.map((item) => (
                      <li>{item}</li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                </article>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- S4 · PROOF -->
    <section class="proof" id="proof">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band band--split">
          <div>
            <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Contact sheet</p>
            <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
              Selected <span class="serif">frames</span>.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <p class="band__note r" style="--d:.1s">
            A handful of stills from recent Meta programs across organic feeds, Advantage+ Reels, enriched catalog carousels, creator Partnership Ads and multilingual avatars.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="sheet">
          {
            samples.map((s, i) => (
              <figure class="shot crop r-clip" style={`--d:${(i % 3) * 0.08}s`}>
                <div class="crop__inner">
                  <img
                    src={s.src}
                    alt={s.alt}
                    width="1024"
                    height="1024"
                    loading="lazy"
                  />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="shot__cap">
                  <span class="shot__kind">{s.kind}</span>
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- S5 · PARTNERSHIP -->
    <section class="source">
      <div class="shell source__grid">
        <div class="source__visual">
          <figure class="source__main crop">
            <div class="crop__inner">
              <img
                src="/Images/meta-hybrid-main.jpg"
                alt="A producer at a wide reference monitor showing the Meta Ads Manager creative library, four columns of Instagram and Facebook ad variants tagged Content, Ads, UGC and Avatar."
                width="1024"
                height="1024"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="source__inset">
            <img
              src="/Images/meta-hybrid-inset.jpg"
              alt="A close cinematic detail of a hand holding a phone vertically against a soft cream background, the screen filled with an Instagram Reels frame including the side rail and bottom navigation of the Reels interface."
              width="1024"
              height="1024"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
          <div class="source__stat">
            <span class="source__stat-num">1 team</span>
            <span class="source__stat-cap">Media buying, creators, commerce and studio AIGC</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="source__body">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Partnership</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Performance discipline, <span class="serif">studio velocity</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="source__lead r" style="--d:.1s">
            The brands pulling ahead on Meta right now are not the ones with the biggest software stack. They are the ones uniting disciplined media buying with an authored creative studio that uses AI for volume.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.16s">
            That is how we are built. Performance media buyers and CAPI engineers sit in the same room as creative directors, retouchers, colorists and AI model trainers. When an ad hook spikes in Ads Manager on Tuesday morning, our studio spins out ten new variations of it by Thursday.
          </p>
          <ul class="creds r" style="--d:.22s">
            {
              credentials.map((c) => (
                <li class="cred">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                  </svg>
                  {c}
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.26s">
            Everything runs on our own infrastructure. Hosting sits in mainland China, Hong Kong, the EU or the US, wherever your data rules point. Your ad accounts, first-party Pixel/CAPI data and custom-trained brand models belong to you.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p source__p--quiet r" style="--d:.3s">
            Some clients hand us the entire Meta operation. Others plug our creative and avatar engine into their in-house media buyers. Both work seamlessly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- APP OR STUDIO -->
    <PlatformAppBand
      pre={'Publish '}
      accent={'yourself'}
      post={' in the app, or have our agency & studio run it.'}
      paras={[
        'You can keep daily organic publishing in-house when you want to. The hubStudio app publishes directly to Facebook Pages and Instagram Professional accounts as Feed posts, Stories or Reels, while our agency and studio team handles Advantage+ media buying, creator whitelisting, catalog commerce and high-volume creative sprints.',
      ]}
      columns={[
        {
          title: 'What your team does in the app',
          items: [
            'Renders images or Reels with AI, or picks approved assets from the library',
            'Drafts captions with AI or writes them by hand',
            'Publishes immediately or schedules across up to 20 accounts per post',
            'Re-purposes one post for LinkedIn, TikTok or X',
          ],
        },
        {
          title: 'What the agency & studio add',
          items: [
            'Full-funnel Meta Ads buying, Advantage+ & CAPI attribution',
            'Creator seeding, Partnership Ads whitelisting & Meta Shops setup',
            'Hero shoots, studio UGC, custom avatars & 50+ tested ad variants',
          ],
        },
      ]}
      shot={appShots.instagram}
      path="/social/instagram/posts"
      actions={[
        { label: 'Create your account', href: APP_SIGNUP, kind: 'primary', external: true },
        { label: 'How publishing works', href: '/app/publish' },
        { label: 'Read the Instagram help', href: '/help/instagram' },
        { label: 'Read the Facebook help', href: '/help/facebook' },
      ]}
    />

    <!-- S6 · PROCESS -->
    <section class="craft" id="craft">
      <div class="shell craft__intro">
        <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>How a Meta program runs</p>
        <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
          From tracking audit<br />to scaled <span class="serif">ROAS</span>.
        </h2>
        <p class="craft__lede r" style="--d:.12s">
          Organic management, Advantage+ media buying, creator whitelisting and high-velocity studio production follow one five-step loop. Most of what decides whether a campaign scales happens in the audit and architecture phase, before a dollar is spent.
        </p>
        <p class="craft__note r" style="--d:.16s">
          Lock the signal and the creative matrix first. Everything after is disciplined iteration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="seq" id="seq">
        <div class="seq__stick">
          <div class="shell seq__stage">
            <div class="seq__nav" aria-label="Process steps">
              {
                processSteps.map((s, i) => (
                  <button
                    class="seq__step"
                    type="button"
                    data-i={i}
                    data-active={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
                  >
                    <span class="seq__step-dot">
                      <span class="seq__step-fill"></span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="seq__step-label">{s.short}</span>
                  </button>
                ))
              }
            </div>

            <div class="seq__panels">
              {
                processSteps.map((s, i) => (
                  <article
                    class="seq__panel"
                    data-panel={i}
                    data-active={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
                  >
                    <figure class="seq__media crop">
                      <div class="crop__inner">
                        <img
                          src={s.image}
                          alt={s.alt}
                          width="1200"
                          height="900"
                          loading="lazy"
                        />
                      </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div class="seq__text">
                      <span class="seq__tier">{s.tier}</span>
                      <h3 class="seq__title">{s.title}</h3>
                      <p class="seq__body">{s.body}</p>
                    </div>
                  </article>
                ))
              }
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- S7 · FAQ -->
    <section class="faq">
      <div class="shell faq__grid">
        <aside class="faq__intro">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Questions</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Before the<br />first <span class="serif">call</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="faq__sub r" style="--d:.1s">
            The things brands ask before we start. If yours is not here, put
            it in the brief.
          </p>
          <div class="r" style="--d:.16s">
            <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Send the brief</Button>
          </div>
          <p class="fig r" style="--d:.2s">Reviewed September 2026</p>
        </aside>

        <div class="acc">
          {
            faqs.map((faq) => (
              <div class="acc__row r">
                <button class="acc__q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                  <span class="acc__qmark">Q</span>
                  <span class="acc__qtext">{faq.q}</span>
                  <span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span></span><span></span>
                  </span>
                </button>
                <div class="acc__a">
                  <div class="acc__a-inner">
                    <p>
                      {faq.link ? (
                        <>
                          {faq.a.split(faq.link.match)[0]}
                          <a href={faq.link.href}>{faq.link.match}</a>
                          {faq.a.split(faq.link.match)[1]}
                        </>
                      ) : (
                        faq.a
                      )}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <WaysToWork tone="white" highlight="studio-app" />

    <!-- S8 · CLOSE -->
    <section class="end">
      <svg class="end__reg" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        <path d="M50 4v92M4 50h92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
      </svg>
      <div class="shell end__inner">
        <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Try us</p>
        <h2 class="end__title r" style="--d:.05s">
          Send the Meta brief.<br />Back in <span class="serif">48 hours</span>.
        </h2>
        <p class="end__p r" style="--d:.12s">
          A producer reads your brief within one business day, and the proposal that comes back gives you a recommendation for each placement, with the scope and the timing. Want to make some of it yourself? Creating an account costs nothing, and you pay only for what you run.
        </p>
        <div class="end__cta r" style="--d:.18s">
          <Button variant="primary" href={BRIEF_URL}>Send a brief</Button>
          <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href={APP_SIGNUP} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Create your account
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="end__signin r" style="--d:.22s">
          Already on hubStudio? <a href={APP_SIGNIN} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sign in</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cbar cbar--end" aria-hidden="true">
        {colourBar.map((c) => <span style={`background:${c}`}></span>)}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page {
    --ink: #0e1633;
    --navy: #0e1f4e;
    --paper: #f0ede9;
    --paper-2: #e7e3dd;
    overflow: clip;
  }
  .shell {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: clamp(22px, 5vw, 60px);
  }

  .prog { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; height: 3px; z-index: 200; pointer-events: none; }
  .prog__bar { display: block; height: 100%; width: 100%; transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: 0 50%; background: var(--brand-orange); }

  .r, .r-clip { --d: 0s; }
  .r { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(26px); transition: opacity 0.7s ease, transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d); }
  .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .r-clip .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 101% 0); transition: clip-path 1.05s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1.12); transition: transform 1.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .r, .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
    .r-clip .crop__inner, .r-clip .crop__inner img { clip-path: none; transform: none; transition: none; }
  }

  .kicker { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .kicker--light { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.66); }
  .kicker__tick { width: 22px; height: 0; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .kicker__sep { color: var(--brand-orange); }

  .dh { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.4vw, 62px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .dh--sm { font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 38px); }
  .serif { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--brand-orange); }

  .crop { position: relative; margin: 0; }
  .crop::before, .crop::after { content: ''; position: absolute; width: 16px; height: 16px; z-index: 2; }
  .crop::before { top: -9px; left: -9px; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-left: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop::after { right: -9px; bottom: 28px; border-right: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop__inner { overflow: hidden; border-radius: 4px; }
  .crop__inner img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .fig { margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }

  .ghost-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-size: var(--type-small); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); }
  .ghost-link svg { width: 19px; height: 19px; transition: transform 0.24s ease-out; }
  .ghost-link:hover svg { transform: translateX(5px); }
  .ghost-link--light { color: var(--text-on-dark); }

  .band { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 5vw, 70px); display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .band--split { max-width: none; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .band--split { grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.82fr; align-items: end; gap: 18px 60px; }
    .band--split > div { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  }
  .band__note { font-size: var(--type-lead); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--text-mute); }

  .cbar { display: flex; height: 12px; }
  .cbar span { flex: 1; }
  .cbar--end { margin-top: clamp(60px, 8vw, 110px); }

  /* Hero */
  .hero { display: grid; background: var(--ink); color: var(--text-on-dark); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .hero__panel { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; padding: clamp(40px, 4.4vw, 72px) clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px); overflow: clip; }
  .hero__reg { position: absolute; width: clamp(240px, 28vw, 420px); right: -12%; bottom: -14%; color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.055); pointer-events: none; }
  .hero__panel-in { position: relative; width: 100%; max-width: 600px; }
  .hero__title { margin-top: 24px; font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(46px, 6.6vw, 92px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.045em; }
  .hero__title .line { display: block; overflow: hidden; padding: 0.22em 0.14em; margin: -0.22em -0.14em; }
  .hero__title .line__i { display: block; transform: translateY(145%); transition: transform 0.9s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
  .hero__title .line:nth-child(1) .line__i { transition-delay: 0.12s; }
  .hero__title .line:nth-child(2) .line__i { transition-delay: 0.22s; }
  .hero__title .line:nth-child(3) .line__i { transition-delay: 0.32s; }
  .hero.in .hero__title .line__i { transform: translateY(0); }
  .hero__title .serif { font-size: 1.04em; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .hero__title .line__i { transform: none; } }
  .hero__tag { margin-top: 26px; font-size: clamp(18px, 1.5vw, 23px); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .hero__tag em { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .hero__lead { margin-top: 20px; display: grid; gap: 13px; max-width: 46ch; }
  .hero__lead p { font-size: var(--type-body); line-height: 1.62; color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.74); }
  .hero__cta { margin-top: 30px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 14px 26px; }
  .hero__meta { margin-top: 34px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1.5px dashed rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.2); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.5); }
  .hero__meta span { color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .hero__visual { position: relative; overflow: hidden; min-height: 58vh; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .hero__visual { min-height: auto; } }
  .hero__visual img { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; transform: scale(1.08); transition: transform 1.5s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
  .hero.in .hero__visual img { transform: scale(1); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .hero__visual img { transform: none; } }
  .hero__chip { position: absolute; left: 18px; bottom: 18px; z-index: 2; display: inline-flex; gap: 8px; padding: 9px 15px; border-radius: var(--radius-pill); background: rgba(14, 22, 51, 0.78); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-on-dark); }
  .hero__chip span { color: var(--brand-orange); }

  /* Why */
  .why { background: var(--ink); color: var(--text-on-dark); padding-block: clamp(80px, 10vw, 150px); }
  .why__top { display: grid; gap: 30px; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .why__top { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 70px; align-items: start; } }
  .why__head .dh { margin-top: 18px; }
  .why__text { display: grid; gap: 16px; align-content: start; padding-top: 6px; }
  .why__text p { font-size: var(--type-body); line-height: 1.62; color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.78); }
  .why__clients { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.6) !important; }
  .why__clients strong { color: var(--text-on-dark); font-weight: 600; }
  .why__shot { margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); }
  .why__shot .crop__inner { aspect-ratio: 16 / 8; }
  .why__shot .fig { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.5); }

  .stats { margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 84px); border-top: 1.5px dashed rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.22); padding-top: clamp(36px, 4vw, 56px); }
  .stats__quote { max-width: 60ch; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(19px, 1.9vw, 25px); line-height: 1.42; color: var(--text-on-dark); }
  .stats__grid { margin-top: 40px; display: grid; gap: 30px; }
  @media (min-width: 720px) { .stats__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; } }
  .stat { display: grid; gap: 5px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1.5px solid rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.16); }
  .stat__num { font-size: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.04em; color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .stat__label { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .stat__note { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.55); }

  /* Coverage */
  .cover { background: var(--paper); padding-block: clamp(80px, 10vw, 150px); }
  .feature { display: grid; gap: 36px; align-items: center; padding-block: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); border-top: 1.5px dashed var(--line-strong); }
  .feature:last-child { border-bottom: 1.5px dashed var(--line-strong); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .feature { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 72px; }
    .feature--rev .feature__media { order: 2; }
  }
  .feature__media .crop__inner { aspect-ratio: 5 / 4; }
  .feature__idx { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .feature__tick { width: 22px; height: 0; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .feature__body .dh { margin-top: 16px; }
  .feature__lead { margin-top: 14px; font-size: var(--type-lead); line-height: 1.42; color: var(--text-ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .feature__p { margin-top: 14px; font-size: var(--type-body); line-height: 1.66; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .feature__scope { margin-top: 24px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-hairline); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .chips { margin-top: 14px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .chip { padding: 8px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-pill); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; transition: background-color 0.18s ease, color 0.18s ease, border-color 0.18s ease; }
  .chip:hover { background: var(--brand-orange); border-color: var(--brand-orange); color: #fff; }

  .matrix { margin-top: clamp(64px, 8vw, 112px); padding-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 84px); border-top: 1.5px dashed var(--line-strong); }
  .matrix__head { max-width: 720px; display: grid; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: clamp(32px, 4vw, 52px); }
  .matrix__sub { font-size: var(--type-body); line-height: 1.62; color: var(--text-mute); }
